## Custody, observed mixed work, and cleanup

Scoring began only after the raw controller finished at **2026-10-26 03:16:23 UTC**, exit 0, with 200 outputs, complete collection, returned shutdown, and no recorded errors. The unchanged supplementary scorer passed exact protocol/source/runtime/config/input, token-to-text, admission and terminal receipt checks for all three runs. Quality uses the original f7/Core/Ascend deterministic/fusion recipe and all 200 frozen cases. Existing model manifest/stat checks were used; weights were not rehashed during this scoring.

The actual raw scheduler receipt matches SHA256 `1293b0f511c0a044f2c84ab5e3b4b3e561c9c707db3cfe35457a6c2ea07ff465`. Every batch has ten recorded P-progress/D-retirement transactions. The frozen supplement independently binds those receipts to admitted request IDs, actual scheduled phases, retirement and batch chronology. This is observed transaction progress, not physical kernel-overlap proof.

Cleanup uses raw's retained terminal/NPU-after records and the owner's prior cleanup verification. The later group run owns the devices; their current occupancy is not evidence against raw cleanup. The raw native log retains **SIGTERM fallback for four workers** after its shutdown grace period. No globally graceful or signal-free shutdown is claimed. The old capsule builder additionally verified the raw producer PID/process group absent and preserved the complete terminal run in a new local capsule for a later explicitly selected batch, excluded from v4.

The unchanged result files are [strict](../raw-quality-v2-strict-result-v1.json) and [supplementary](../raw-quality-v2-supplementary-result-v1.json). [review.json](review.json) binds their identities, exact CLI argv, the retained logs, all seven detailed comparisons, original gates, per-case status sets and mixed coverage. `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` prevented imports from writing cache files into frozen inputs; scorer argv remained exactly as prescribed. No new sampling, model/device operation, source edit or GitHub mutation was performed for this review.
